router: replace the bypass-mark rule trio with one inverted rule

In Android, the pref 10/30/50 bypass-mark rules fire before netd's
per-network/per-uid policy rules at pref >=10000 and short-circuit
them. Install a single inverted-fwmark rule at pref 70 instead, so
bypass-marked packets fall through to whatever sits below us.

diff --git a/wgengine/router/osrouter/router_linux.go b/wgengine/router/osrouter/router_linux.go
index c8b31d0..2332805 100644
--- a/wgengine/router/osrouter/router_linux.go
+++ b/wgengine/router/osrouter/router_linux.go
@@ -1580,51 +1580,20 @@ func mustRouteTable(num int) RouteTable {
